## What is wrong (one paragraph)
Two routes answer `403 "Caller has no tenant"` when the caller HAS a tenant. `principalScope(user)` (`rateLimitScope.ts:112-127`) returns
`null` for THREE reasons — no claim to scope by (tenant AND user/sub all absent), a MALFORMED tenant claim (present but not a non-blank string),
or a MALFORMED user/`sub` claim — and both call sites collapse all three into one message: `/api/rate-limit/check` at `index.ts:1373-1381`
(`scope === null` → 403 at line 1379) and `/api/rate-limit/reset` at `index.ts:1486-1491` (`explicitScope(...)` null → 403 at line 1489;
its body fields are already schema-refused at 1468–1471, so a null here comes from the caller's principal). **Fix (the ticket's fix-shape):
split it — "no claim to scope by" and "present but unusable" say different things.** At each site, read the principal once: if ANY of
`tenantId` / `userId` / `sub` is present (not `undefined`/`null`) the null means "present but unusable"; otherwise "no tenant". NOT in this task:
lines 752 and 803 (they test the tenant claim DIRECTLY and their message is literally true — the ticket says so), `rateLimitScope.ts`,
the 400 at line 1470 (Part A). No new imports.

